# compose 서비스로 실행합니다 ``giteamcpupstream`` 역할의 자신의 네트워크에만, 그래서 아무것도 하지만 어댑터 도달.
# 그것은 답변 ``initialize`` 이름 * ``tools/list`` 자체의 credential을 보유하고 각 클라이언트가 공급하는
# 것을 기대하기 때문에 어떤 caller에 Gitea 요청당 토큰은 직접 노출되지 않습니다. 어댑터는 인증된 것입니다: 클라이언트는
# ``mcp_bearer`` 자격 및 거절 401 그렇지 않으면 어댑터는 minted를 나타냅니다. Gitea 토큰 업스트림
# ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``·.
# sidecar runs as compose service ``giteamcpupstream`` on the role’s own
# network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers
# ``initialize`` and ``tools/list`` to any caller because it holds no
# credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per
# request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what
# authenticates: a client presents the ``mcp_bearer`` credential and is
# refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token
# upstream via ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``.
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar runs as compose service ``giteamcpupstream`` on the role’s own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers ``initialize`` and ``tools/list`` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the ``mcp_bearer`` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``."
msgstr ""

# 서비스로 실행합니다 `giteamcpupstream` 역할의 자신의 네트워크에만, 그래서 아무것도 하지만 어댑터 도달. 그것은 답변
# `initialize` 이름 * `tools/list` 자체의 credential을 보유하고 각 클라이언트가 공급하는 것을 기대하기
# 때문에 어떤 caller에 Gitea 요청당 토큰은 직접 노출되지 않습니다. 어댑터는 인증된 것입니다: 클라이언트는
# `mcp_bearer` 자격 및 거절 401 그렇지 않으면 어댑터는 minted를 나타냅니다. Gitea 토큰 업스트림
# `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`·.
# id="1"></x> The <x id="2"></x> sidecar runs as compose service <x
# id="3"></x> on the role's own network only, so nothing but the <x
# id="4"></x> reaches it. It <x id="5"></x> and <x id="6"></x> to any caller
# because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply
# a <x id="7"></x> token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose
# directly. The <x id="8"></x> is what authenticates: a client presents the <x
# id="9"></x> credential and is refused with <x id="10"></x> otherwise, and
# the <x id="11"></x> presents the minted <x id="12"></x> token upstream via
# <x id="13"></x>.
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The `gitea-mcp` sidecar runs as compose service `giteamcpupstream` on the role's own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers `initialize` and `tools/list` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the `mcp_bearer` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`."
msgstr ""

