# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Admin / role model = both** (operator: \"admin anlegen wenn nicht oidc sonst claim mapping\"), implemented within Semaphore's constraints: (a) a **break-glass local admin** is always seeded via `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN*` with a dedicated `breakglass` login + dedicated email — reachable via the form only when LDAP is off; (b) when SSO is enabled the role creates the Keycloak administrator as an **external admin** at deploy time (`semaphore user add --admin --external`), so the OIDC callback (matches by email, accepts only external users) elevates that operator to admin. Upstream has no claim→role mapping, so this deploy-time external-admin seed is the \"smallest reconciliation step\"."
msgstr "**Admin / 역할 모델 = 모두** (통신수: \"admin anlegen wenn nicht oidc sonst 주장 맵핑\"), Semaphore의 제약 내에서 구현: (한국어) 한국어 **Break-glass 현지 관리자** 항상 Seeded `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN*` 관련 기사 `breakglass` 로그인 + 전용 이메일 — LDAP가 꺼질 때만 양식을 통해 도달 가능; (₢ 킹) SSO가 활성화되면 역할은 Keycloak 관리자로 **외부 admin** 배포 시간 (`semaphore user add --admin --external`), 그래서 OIDC 콜백 (이메일과 일치하여 외부 사용자 만 허용) 관리자에게 그 연산자를 높입니다. 업스트림은 주장이 없습니다.→로드 맵핑, 그래서이 배치 시간 외부 관리자 씨앗은 \"가장 작은 reconciliation 단계\"·."

msgid "**Admin Accounts from the Administrator Group:** [`files/php/rbac/reconcile_admin_users.php`](./files/php/rbac/reconcile_admin_users.php) activates the Magento admin accounts of the `administrator` group members and deactivates every other admin account; the platform administrator stays untouched. [`tasks/04_rbac.yml`](./tasks/04_rbac.yml) registers it as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/), which runs it in the PHP container at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Accounts from the Administrator Group:** ```files/php/rbac/reconcile_admin_users.php`` <./files/php/rbac/reconcile_admin_users.php>`__ activates the Magento admin accounts of the ``administrator`` group members and deactivates every other admin account; the platform administrator stays untouched. ```tasks/04_rbac.yml`` <./tasks/04_rbac.yml>`__ registers it as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__, which runs it in the PHP container at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Backend Gate:** with SSO the gate admits every realm user to the storefront, while ``sso.oauth2.restricted_locations`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ admits only members of the ``administrator`` group to the backend path ``services.magento.backend_frontname``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Backend Gate:** with SSO the gate admits every realm user to the storefront, while `sso.oauth2.restricted_locations` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) admits only members of the `administrator` group to the backend path `services.magento.backend_frontname`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Console Roles:** The groups ``user-manager``, ``auditor`` and ``impersonator`` under ``/roles/web-app-keycloak`` grant user management, read-only auditing and impersonation in the application realm. Each role lists its ``realm-management`` client roles under ``realm_management`` in `rbac.yml <meta/rbac.yml>`__. ``realm-admin`` stays with the local bootstrap account. A user manager can change group memberships, which includes every application role group, so grant ``user-manager`` only to people trusted with every application role."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Console Roles:** The groups `user-manager`, `auditor` and `impersonator` under `/roles/web-app-keycloak` grant user management, read-only auditing and impersonation in the application realm. Each role lists its `realm-management` client roles under `realm_management` in [rbac.yml](meta/rbac.yml). `realm-admin` stays with the local bootstrap account. A user manager can change group memberships, which includes every application role group, so grant `user-manager` only to people trusted with every application role."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag From RBAC:** [files/python/rbac_sync.py](./files/python/rbac_sync.py) sets the Pixelfed admin flag on the members of the `administrator` role group, matched by username, e-mail or OIDC mapping, and clears it on every other account. It runs as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) against the database container at every deploy and on its timer. With `sso`, the listener [files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php](./files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php), mounted into `app/Listeners` where Laravel's event discovery registers it, applies the same flag at every OIDC sign-in from the `administrator` group in the groups claim, which [files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php](./files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php) reads off the userinfo response on its way through `UserOidcService`; a group change therefore reaches the account at its next sign-in, and a new member holds the flag from its first one. The administrator created through artisan keeps the flag."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag From RBAC:** `files/python/rbac_sync.py <./files/python/rbac_sync.py>`__ sets the Pixelfed admin flag on the members of the ``administrator`` role group, matched by username, e-mail or OIDC mapping, and clears it on every other account. It runs as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ against the database container at every deploy and on its timer. With ``sso``, the listener `files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php <./files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php>`__, mounted into ``app/Listeners`` where Laravel’s event discovery registers it, applies the same flag at every OIDC sign-in from the ``administrator`` group in the groups claim, which `files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php <./files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php>`__ reads off the userinfo response on its way through ``UserOidcService``; a group change therefore reaches the account at its next sign-in, and a new member holds the flag from its first one. The administrator created through artisan keeps the flag."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag and Profile at Every SAML Sign-In:** the same extension sets ``is_admin`` from the ``administrator`` group and writes first and last name, work and mobile phone, title, department and address from the assertion (``SUITECRM_SAML_PROFILE_COLUMNS`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) into the user record."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag and Profile at Every SAML Sign-In:** the same extension sets `is_admin` from the `administrator` group and writes first and last name, work and mobile phone, title, department and address from the assertion (`SUITECRM_SAML_PROFILE_COLUMNS` in [`vars/main.yml`](./vars/main.yml)) into the user record."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag from the Administrator Group:** with SSO or LDAP, [`files/php/reconcile_admins.php`](./files/php/reconcile_admins.php) sets `is_admin` for the members of the `administrator` group and clears it for every other user; the platform administrator keeps it. It runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer, so an account the SAML or LDAP sign-in creates later gets the flag on the next run."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag from the Administrator Group:** with SSO or LDAP, ```files/php/reconcile_admins.php`` <./files/php/reconcile_admins.php>`__ sets ``is_admin`` for the members of the ``administrator`` group and clears it for every other user; the platform administrator keeps it. It runs as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer, so an account the SAML or LDAP sign-in creates later gets the flag on the next run."
msgstr ""

