msgid "**Break-glass access:** with the ``oic`` realm, ``/login`` always hands over to Keycloak and Jenkins renders no local form. The break-glass runs on the host: override ``services.jenkins.login.method.sso.enabled: false`` in the inventory and redeploy, which renders the ``ldap`` or ``local`` realm, or, when no deploy can run, replace the ``securityRealm`` block of the mounted ``casc.yaml`` in the role’s instance directory with the ``local`` realm of the platform administrator and restart the container, since JCasC applies the file at startup. The API token ```files/mcp-api-token.groovy`` <./files/mcp-api-token.groovy>`__ mints belongs to the MCP credential owner, not to an administrator, so it is no break-glass."
