# integrations auto-enable 와 그들의 파트너.** `enabled` 옵션 및 기본값은 `false` 이름 *
# `required: true` 설정입니다. 서비스 MUST를 연결하는 애드온은 그 서비스에서 효과적인 활성화를 유도합니다.
# `enabled` 계정 만들기 (절대 복제 그룹 멤버쉽 표현), 그래서 deliberately-wired 크로스로드 통합은 파트너 역할이
# 공동 배포 될 때마다 자동으로 활성화 (`services.<target>.enabled` 진정한) 그리고 그렇지 않으면 유지. addon
# 필요는 선언됩니다 `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` 자주 묻는 질문 `lookup('config',
# application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')` (12 월 4): 조작자가 비밀을 입력해야 할 수있는
# 자동 생성, 또는 동일한 자격 메커니즘의 수동 기반 경로를 통해 공급. 별도의 opt-in 예외가 없습니다. 자동 사용
# 가능-partner 보유 및 운영자 중심의 자격 해결 `credentials` 다른 것 처럼. 이 자동 사용 가능한-partner 규칙은
# 업데이트-automation-discovered addons에서 명백합니다 (12 월 10), 추가된 hard-off.
# '12']
# deliberately-wired integrations auto-disable with their partner.** `enabled`
# is optional and defaults to `false` unless `required: true` is set. An addon
# that bridges a service MUST derive its effective auto-enablement from that
# service's `enabled` flag ( never a duplicated group-membership expression),
# so a deliberately-wired cross-role integration activates automatically
# whenever its partner role is co-deployed (`services.<target>.enabled` is
# true) and stays off otherwise. Any credential an addon needs is declared in
# `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` and read via `lookup('config',
# application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')` (Decision 4): auto-generated
# where possible, or supplied through the same credentials mechanism's
# manual-entry path where the operator must enter the secret. There is no
# separate opt-in exception: auto-enable-with-partner holds, and an
# operator-entered credential resolves through `credentials` like any other.
# This auto-enable-with-partner rule is distinct from (Decision 10), which are
# added hard-off.
msgid "**Enable state defaults to off; deliberately-wired integrations auto-enable with their partner.** `enabled` is optional and defaults to `false` unless `required: true` is set. An addon that bridges a service MUST derive its effective enablement from that service's `enabled` flag (never a duplicated group-membership expression), so a deliberately-wired cross-role integration activates automatically whenever its partner role is co-deployed (`services.<target>.enabled` is true) and stays off otherwise. Any credential an addon needs is declared in `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` and read via `lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')` (Decision 4): auto-generated where possible, or supplied through the same credentials mechanism's manual-entry path where the operator must enter the secret. There is no separate opt-in exception: auto-enable-with-partner holds, and an operator-entered credential resolves through `credentials` like any other. This auto-enable-with-partner rule is distinct from update-automation-discovered addons (Decision 10), which are added hard-off."
msgstr ""

