msgid "**Own site**: only when `WORDPRESS_SITE_OWNER_ENABLED` is `true`. For a member of `/roles/web-app-wordpress/site-owner` the mapper finds the site `<login>.<host of WORDPRESS_SITE_OWNER_BASE_URL>`. It creates the site with the member as administrator when it is missing, recording the `sub` claim in the site meta `infinito_site_owner_subject`, restores it when it is archived and keeps the member its administrator. For a user outside the group it archives that site, keeping its content. It only acts on a site whose recorded subject matches, or on a site that `infinito_rbac_reserve_own_site()` reserved for the login through `infinito_site_owner_login` at deploy. The first sign-in claims a reserved site: it records the subject and removes every other member, the deploy's interim administrator included. The per-site loop skips the own site. A login the member label rule refuses, a login claim other than the account's login, a missing subject or a foreign site is logged and skips only this step, so the sign-in still completes. At deploy, `infinito_rbac_archive_reserved_sites_of_former_members()` archives every own site whose login is no longer an inventory member and ends its owner's sessions."
msgstr ""

