# Unauthenticated 요청은 Symfony 방화벽의 SAML 엔트리 포인트를 기록합니다. Keycloak; assertion는
# 뒤에 옵니다 `/saml/acs` 그리고 실제 설정 SuiteCRM 세션, 그래서 앱은 로그아웃 컨트롤을 포함한 자체 인증 UI를
# 렌더링합니다. 계정은 assertion에서 첫 번째 로그인에 생성됩니다. (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), 그리고 IdP 서명
# 증명서는에서 읽습니다 Keycloak진정한 감정가
# [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh)
# 부트에서, Tor SOCKS 프록시를 통해 발행자는 양파이기 때문에 `.onion` 발행자는 직접 신뢰할 수 없습니다. `/auth`
# 로컬 Break-glass 로그인으로 도달 할 수 있습니다.
# Keycloak(`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)),
# not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony
# firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion
# comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the
# app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts
# are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the
# IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by
# [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at
# boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a
# `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the
# local break-glass login.
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr ""

