#, python-format
msgid "**WordPress options from the configuration:** `WORDPRESS_OPTIONS` in [main.yml](vars/main.yml) is one map: `admin_email` is the platform administrator's email, `blogname` is the design title while the `design` service is on, and the `config.options` of the `freedomtranslate-wp` addon join while that addon is on; `services.wordpress.options` from [services.yml](meta/services.yml) and the inventory overlay them, so an inventory entry wins. Every entry is written with `wp option update` whenever WordPress stores a different value, and a write that changes the stored value flushes the rewrite rules. Every deploy therefore sets `admin_email`, and `blogname` while the design is on, back to the configured value: a change made in wp-admin is reverted. An inventory sets any option through `applications.web-app-wordpress.services.wordpress.options.<name>`: the key carries `# nocheck: inventory-open-subtree`, so the inventory validator accepts names [services.yml](meta/services.yml) does not declare. Options the role computes or WordPress manages (`WORDPRESS_OPTIONS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE` in [main.yml](vars/main.yml)) and keys that name a secret are refused. `permalink_structure` is pinned to `/blog/%year%/%monthnum%/%day%/%postname%/`, the structure the blog published its post URLs under."
msgstr ""

#, python-format
msgid "**WordPress options from the configuration:** ``WORDPRESS_OPTIONS`` in `main.yml <vars/main.yml>`__ is one map: ``admin_email`` is the platform administrator’s email, ``blogname`` is the design title while the ``design`` service is on, and the ``config.options`` of the ``freedomtranslate-wp`` addon join while that addon is on; ``services.wordpress.options`` from `services.yml <meta/services.yml>`__ and the inventory overlay them, so an inventory entry wins. Every entry is written with ``wp option update`` whenever WordPress stores a different value, and a write that changes the stored value flushes the rewrite rules. Every deploy therefore sets ``admin_email``, and ``blogname`` while the design is on, back to the configured value: a change made in wp-admin is reverted. An inventory sets any option through ``applications.web-app-wordpress.services.wordpress.options.<name>``: the key carries ``# nocheck: inventory-open-subtree``, so the inventory validator accepts names `services.yml <meta/services.yml>`__ does not declare. Options the role computes or WordPress manages (``WORDPRESS_OPTIONS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE`` in `main.yml <vars/main.yml>`__) and keys that name a secret are refused. ``permalink_structure`` is pinned to ``/blog/%year%/%monthnum%/%day%/%postname%/``, the structure the blog published its post URLs under."
msgstr ""

