msgid "An answer about the item is ``OPEN`` or ``CLOSED``, and HTTP 404 or 410 is ``MISSING``. A timeout, a connection error, HTTP 429 and a 5xx answer are retried with a doubling pause before they count. An exhausted rate limit (a 429 that survives the retries, or a 403 that carries ``X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`` or ``Retry-After``) is ``RATE_LIMITED``, with the reset time the tracker announced. Everything else that still fails is ``UNVERIFIED``: a network error, an auth wall, any other status, a body that is not a JSON object and a state the adapter does not know. A tracker that could not be asked therefore never reads as one that said the item is still open."
