# `mcp.enabled` 이름 * Baserow's canonical vhost는 여전히 대답 `401 Endpoint not
# found.` 에 의해 `/mcp/<key>/sse`, 이미지가 ASGI root unconditionally에 MCP 앱을 마운트하고
# flag only는 endpoint 레코드가 제공되는지 여부를 판단합니다. 잘못된 자격은 여전히 표면입니다, 어떤 장애인 상태
# assertion 말한다 그리고 왜 실패. 동일한 라우팅은 MCP가 *에 의해*: 어댑터는 4 개의 15 개의 업스트림 도구가 좁아서
# 공개적으로 routed native path walks가 끝점 키를 들고 누군가를 위해 4 개의 14 개로 직진합니다.
# `web-app-homeassistant` 같은 모양을 가지고, `exposure: internal` 표면은 공개 vhost에
# 도달합니다. 더 알아보기 404 컨테이너 네트워크에 도달 할 수 있습니다. `internal` 항상 의미한다.
# '14', '15', '4']
# was worth the deploy. With `mcp.enabled` false, Baserow's canonical vhost
# still answered `401 Endpoint not found.` on `/mcp/<key>/sse`, because the
# image mounts the MCP app on the ASGI root unconditionally and the flag only
# governs whether an endpoint record is provisioned. A refused credential is
# still a surface, which is what the disabled-state assertion says and why it
# failed. The same routing has a sharper edge while MCP is *on*: the adapter
# narrows fourteen upstream tools to four, and a publicly routed native path
# walks straight past it to all fourteen for anyone holding the endpoint key.
# `web-app-homeassistant` had the same shape, an `exposure: internal` surface
# reachable on its public vhost. Both now 404 there and stay reachable on the
# container network, which is what `internal` was always supposed to mean.
msgid "Anything else gets `return 404`, and finding that out was worth the deploy. With `mcp.enabled` false, Baserow's canonical vhost still answered `401 Endpoint not found.` on `/mcp/<key>/sse`, because the image mounts the MCP app on the ASGI root unconditionally and the flag only governs whether an endpoint record is provisioned. A refused credential is still a surface, which is what the disabled-state assertion says and why it failed. The same routing has a sharper edge while MCP is *on*: the adapter narrows fourteen upstream tools to four, and a publicly routed native path walks straight past it to all fourteen for anyone holding the endpoint key. `web-app-homeassistant` had the same shape, an `exposure: internal` surface reachable on its public vhost. Both now 404 there and stay reachable on the container network, which is what `internal` was always supposed to mean."
msgstr ""

