msgid "Both layers are exhaustive over what the repository declares, which is exactly why the backlog lives outside them: an **open** pair, where a verified upstream plugin exists but nothing declares it, has no generated representation at all. Moving a pair from open to declared is the per-role upstream survey, and that survey is itself an acceptance criterion of this requirement (a MediaWiki deep-dive, for instance, added `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio and an LLM editor→openwebui). [027-integration-matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) states where each layer's truth lives and why no frozen copy of the map is kept."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both layers are process-wide in-process caches. They intentionally do NOT track on-disk file mtimes; CLI tools are short-lived and the assumption \"the on-disk file does not change while my process runs\" holds. The single exception is `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, which writes through and evicts the cached entry for the path it just wrote so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."
msgstr "두 레이어는 프로세스 전체 in-process 캐시입니다. 그들은 의도적으로 on-disk 파일 mtimes를 추적하지 않습니다; CLI 도구는 부족하고 가정 \"on-disk 파일은 변경되지 않습니다.\" 회사연혁 단일 예외는 `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, 을 작성하고 evicts the cached entry for the path it just written so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."

msgid "Both markers are looked for on the construct's own line and across every contiguous comment line directly above it, in either order. This is the placement for an exemption that has to say *why*: the reason rarely fits beside the value, so it is written as a comment block above it, and :func:`is_suppressed_at` would only see the last line of that block."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both modes MUST keep a minimum age that outlasts every timeout of the application, so nothing an in-flight operation still writes is removed. `pressure` MAY only shorten ages, never drop them to \"now\". The one exception is a native command that drops a cache the application regenerates on demand, such as Nextcloud's `occ preview:cleanup`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both name a Frappe doctype the image already ships, and the per-addon hooks [`tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml`](./tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml) and [`tasks/addons/email_account.yml`](./tasks/addons/email_account.yml) apply it through the bench python scripts [`oidc_settings.py`](./files/python/apply/oidc_settings.py) and [`email_account.py`](./files/python/apply/email_account.py)."
