# 운반합니다. 비어 있는 ``access_grants`` is not “nobody”: Open WebUI는 모든 관리자로 그것을
# 읽습니다. ``mcp`` 그룹. 이름 * ``ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`` 모든 시작에 대한 env 권한이
# 다시 만들어, 활성화-but-ungranted 항목은 첫 번째 프로비저닝 실행 전에 모든 관리자에 액세스하고 모든 베어 컨테이너 재시작
# 후. 장애인 입장은 전혀 제공되지 않습니다, 그래서 fallback는 너무 많지 않습니다.
# one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty ``access_grants`` is
# not “nobody”: Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider
# than the ``mcp`` group. Since ``ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`` makes the
# env authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would
# hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and
# after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so
# the fallback is no access rather than too much.
msgid "Entries render **disabled**, and the task enables each one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty ``access_grants`` is not “nobody”: Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider than the ``mcp`` group. Since ``ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`` makes the env authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so the fallback is no access rather than too much."
msgstr ""

# 운반합니다. 비어 있는 `access_grants` 아니다. "nobody": Open WebUI는 모든 관리자로 읽습니다. `mcp`
# 그룹. 이름 * `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false` 모든 시작에 대한 env 권한이 다시 만들어,
# 활성화-but-ungranted 항목은 첫 번째 프로비저닝 실행 전에 모든 관리자에 액세스하고 모든 베어 컨테이너 재시작 후. 장애인
# 입장은 전혀 제공되지 않습니다, 그래서 fallback는 너무 많지 않습니다.
# one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty `access_grants` is
# not "nobody": Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider
# than the `mcp` group. Since `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false` makes the env
# authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would
# hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and
# after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so
# the fallback is no access rather than too much.
msgid "Entries render **disabled**, and the task enables each one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty `access_grants` is not \"nobody\": Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider than the `mcp` group. Since `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false` makes the env authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so the fallback is no access rather than too much."
msgstr ""

