# 그래서이 모듈은 표준 라이브러리에 머물. 또한 자체 패키지 내부에 머물 : Dockerfile은 이미지 옆에 복사
# ``utils/__init__.py`` 이름 * ``utils/install/__init__.py`` 그리고 아무것도 다른, 그래서 다른
# 사람을 수입 ``utils`` submodule 상승 ``ModuleNotFoundError`` 그것을 실행 층에서. 요구 사항 파일이
# 읽는 것은이 저장소의 자체이며 하나의 모양을 붙 잡습니다. ``collections:`` 이름 * ``- name:`` 선택 사항
# ``version:``. 그 모양과 일치하지 않는 라인은 콜러가 불쾌하고 설치로 치료하는 항목이 손상되지 않는 것을 남깁니다.
# interpreter before any dependency is installed, so this module stays on the
# standard library. It also stays inside its own package: the Dockerfile
# copies it into the image beside ``utils/__init__.py`` and
# ``utils/install/__init__.py`` and nothing else, so importing any other
# ``utils`` submodule raises ``ModuleNotFoundError`` in the layer that runs
# it. The requirements files it reads are this repository's own and hold one
# shape: a ``collections:`` list of ``- name:`` entries with an optional
# ``version:``. A line that does not match that shape leaves the entry
# unpinned, which the caller treats as unsatisfied and installs.
msgid "Imported by the lint bootstrap, which runs on a bare interpreter before any dependency is installed, so this module stays on the standard library. It also stays inside its own package: the Dockerfile copies it into the image beside ``utils/__init__.py`` and ``utils/install/__init__.py`` and nothing else, so importing any other ``utils`` submodule raises ``ModuleNotFoundError`` in the layer that runs it. The requirements files it reads are this repository's own and hold one shape: a ``collections:`` list of ``- name:`` entries with an optional ``version:``. A line that does not match that shape leaves the entry unpinned, which the caller treats as unsatisfied and installs."
