# repository-ref updaters 이제 단일 결합 PR 대신 영향을받는 역할 당 하나의 풀 요청을 열고, 그들은 최신에 대한
# 디퓨트를 recompute *이름 **실행 시간 — 업데이트 작업 체크 아웃 *이름** 트리거 커밋 보다는 오히려, 그래서 더 긴
# proposes 이미 merged 변화 또는 뭉치 관련 역할. 각 역할은 자신의 지점을 가져옵니다 (*업데이트<type>- -
# -<role>- - -<date>- - -<fingerprint>*) and a role-scoped 중복 검사, 동안
# *기술-lock.json* updater deliberately는 단일 PR을 유지합니다. 이름 * [업데이트 워크플로우
# 카탈로그](docs/contributing/tools/github/actions/workflows.md)·.
# *skills-lock.json* updater deliberately는 단일 PR을 유지합니다. 이름 * [업데이트 워크플로우
# repository-ref updaters now open one pull request per affected role instead
# of a single combined PR, and they recompute the diff against the latest
# *main* at run time — the update jobs check out *main* rather than the
# triggering commit, so a queued or stale run no longer proposes
# already-merged changes or bundles unrelated roles. Each role gets its own
# branch (*update/<type>-<role>-<date>-<fingerprint>*) and a role-scoped
# duplicate check, while the *skills-lock.json* updater deliberately stays a
# single PR. See [the update workflow
# catalog](docs/contributing/tools/github/actions/workflows.md).
msgid "Per-role update PRs: the Docker-image-version and repository-ref updaters now open one pull request per affected role instead of a single combined PR, and they recompute the diff against the latest *main* at run time — the update jobs check out *main* rather than the triggering commit, so a queued or stale run no longer proposes already-merged changes or bundles unrelated roles. Each role gets its own branch (*update/<type>-<role>-<date>-<fingerprint>*) and a role-scoped duplicate check, while the *skills-lock.json* updater deliberately stays a single PR. See [the update workflow catalog](docs/contributing/tools/github/actions/workflows.md)."
msgstr ""

