msgid "The pin does not by itself carry the OIDC back-channel on an onion node. libcurl refuses a `.onion` name in `Curl_resolv()` before it reads its own cache or `/etc/hosts` (curl 8.5.0 `lib/hostip.c:694-701`), so the token, JWKS and userinfo calls `auth_oidc` makes through Moodle's `\\curl` never leave the container. `MOODLE_OIDC_SOCKS_PROXY` therefore exports `http_proxy`, `https_proxy` and `no_proxy` into `.env/env` whenever the Keycloak domain ends in `.onion`: libcurl reads the lowercase names, `socks5h://` hands the name to Tor to resolve, and on a clearnet issuer the three keys are not rendered at all. The FPM pool keeps `clear_env = no`, which is what puts the container environment in front of libcurl, and only the `moodle` and `cron` services read `.env/env`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pin does not by itself carry the OIDC back-channel on an onion node. libcurl refuses a ``.onion`` name in ``Curl_resolv()`` before it reads its own cache or ``/etc/hosts`` (curl 8.5.0 ``lib/hostip.c:694-701``), so the token, JWKS and userinfo calls ``auth_oidc`` makes through Moodle’s ``\\curl`` never leave the container. ``MOODLE_OIDC_SOCKS_PROXY`` therefore exports ``http_proxy``, ``https_proxy`` and ``no_proxy`` into ``.env/env`` whenever the Keycloak domain ends in ``.onion``: libcurl reads the lowercase names, ``socks5h://`` hands the name to Tor to resolve, and on a clearnet issuer the three keys are not rendered at all. The FPM pool keeps ``clear_env = no``, which is what puts the container environment in front of libcurl, and only the ``moodle`` and ``cron`` services read ``.env/env``."
msgstr ""

