# [build_ldap_role_entries](../../../../roles/svc-db-openldap/filter_plugins/build_ldap_role_entries.py)
# 또한 per-application을 방출 `groupOfNames` 회사 소개
# `cn=<application_id>,ou=roles,...` 이름 * `member` 속성 참조 해당 응용 프로그램의 모든 역할 그룹,
# 그래서 LDAP 전용 소비자는 여전히 계층을 탐색 할 수 있습니다. Keycloak은 그 컨테이너에 의존하지 않습니다; 그것은 재구성
# `/roles/<application_id>/<role_name>` per-application mappers를 통해 (더 보기)·.
# would be:  --- The producer
# also emits a per-application `groupOfNames` container
# `cn=<application_id>,ou=roles,...` whose `member` attribute references every
# role group of that application, so an LDAP-only consumer can still navigate
# the hierarchy. Keycloak does not rely on those containers; it reconstructs
# `/roles/<application_id>/<role_name>` via per-application mappers (see
# below). ---  Note: I've kept the formatting the same as the original text.
msgid "The producer [build_ldap_role_entries](../../../../roles/svc-db-openldap/filter_plugins/build_ldap_role_entries.py) also emits a per-application `groupOfNames` container `cn=<application_id>,ou=roles,...` whose `member` attribute references every role group of that application, so an LDAP-only consumer can still navigate the hierarchy. Keycloak does not rely on those containers; it reconstructs `/roles/<application_id>/<role_name>` via per-application mappers (see below)."
msgstr ""

