# 보유256-GCM-encrypted in the process-local cache, and drops a usable PDS
# session into the social-app’s local storage so end users never see the 종합적인
# 자격 증명.
# gates the web client through Keycloak 이름 * ``web-app-keycloak`` SSO 프록시
msgid "This role deploys a self-hosted Bluesky stack on Docker Compose. It runs the official PDS container as the user-data layer, builds the upstream ``@bluesky-social/social-app`` web client as the user-facing UI, and adds an in-role login-broker sidecar that gates the web client through Keycloak via ``web-app-keycloak``\\ ’s SSO-proxy sidecar. The broker auto-provisions PDS accounts for incoming OIDC users, holds the synthesised app-password AES-256-GCM-encrypted in a process-local cache, and drops a usable PDS session into the social-app’s local storage so end users never see the synthesised credential."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys a single self-built, standard-library container in Compose and Swarm. The container wraps the committed, stack-free control-plane libraries under ``utils/orchestrator/`` and ``utils/agents/`` and exposes them over an OpenAPI instance API. The audit trail persists to ``svc-db-postgres``; accounts are created with the provisioner’s own rights against Keycloak and the LDAP backend it federates. A registration names an instance by a public key, provisioning is an owner-approved ask, every write rests on a live lease, and audit entries carry no secret values."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys a single self-built, standard-library container in Compose and Swarm. The container wraps the committed, stack-free control-plane libraries under ``utils/orchestrator/`` and exposes them over an OpenAPI management API. Checkpoints and the audit trail live in ``svc-db-postgres``; model nodes relay through the shared ``svc-ai-litellm`` gateway with the orchestrator’s own virtual key. The orchestrator reaches each agent workspace through a per-workspace token, so one workspace cannot reach another, and graph state carries secret handles, never secret values."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys a single self-built, standard-library container in Compose and Swarm. The container wraps the committed, stack-free control-plane libraries under `utils/orchestrator/` and `utils/agents/` and exposes them over an OpenAPI instance API. The audit trail persists to `svc-db-postgres`; accounts are created with the provisioner's own rights against Keycloak and the LDAP backend it federates. A registration names an instance by a public key, provisioning is an owner-approved ask, every write rests on a live lease, and audit entries carry no secret values."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys a single self-built, standard-library container in Compose and Swarm. The container wraps the committed, stack-free control-plane libraries under `utils/orchestrator/` and exposes them over an OpenAPI management API. Checkpoints and the audit trail live in `svc-db-postgres`; model nodes relay through the shared `svc-ai-litellm` gateway with the orchestrator's own virtual key. The orchestrator reaches each agent workspace through a per-workspace token, so one workspace cannot reach another, and graph state carries secret handles, never secret values."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys an Nginx vhost behind the project's standard reverse proxy and exposes the canonical `mirror` service so that other roles can consume it through `services.mirror`. The vhost proxies path-prefixed requests (`/<origin-host>/<path>`) to exactly the external origins aggregated from all deployed applications' `server.csp.whitelist` declarations; every other upstream is refused. When an application enables the `mirror` service, the shared body filter rewrites the external asset URLs in its HTML responses to the mirror domain, and the CSP builder allows the mirror origin in the asset directives."
msgstr "이 역할은 프로젝트의 표준 역 프록시 뒤에 Nginx vhost를 배포하고 canonical 노출 `mirror` 다른 역할이 그것을 통해 소비 할 수 있도록 서비스 `services.mirror`. vhost 프록시 path-prefixed 요청 (`/<origin-host>/<path>`) 모든 배치된 응용 프로그램에서 정확히 외부 기원을 집계 `server.csp.whitelist` 선언; 다른 모든 업스트림은 거부됩니다. 신청할 때 `mirror` 서비스, 공유 바디 필터는 HTML 응답에서 미러 도메인에 대한 외부 자산 URL을 다시 작성하고 CSP 빌더는 자산 지침의 미러 소스를 허용합니다."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys an Nginx vhost behind the project’s standard reverse proxy and exposes the canonical ``mirror`` service so that other roles can consume it through ``services.mirror``. The vhost proxies path-prefixed requests (``/<origin-host>/<path>``) to exactly the external origins aggregated from all deployed applications’ ``server.csp.whitelist`` declarations; every other upstream is refused. When an application enables the ``mirror`` service, the shared body filter rewrites the external asset URLs in its HTML responses to the mirror domain, and the CSP builder allows the mirror origin in the asset directives."
msgstr "이 역할은 프로젝트의 표준 역 프록시 뒤에 Nginx vhost를 배포하고 canonical 노출 ``mirror`` 다른 역할이 그것을 통해 소비 할 수 있도록 서비스 ``services.mirror``. vhost 프록시 path-prefixed 요청 (``/<origin-host>/<path>``) 모든 배포된 응용 프로그램에서 정확히 외부의 근원에 ``server.csp.whitelist`` 선언; 다른 모든 업스트림은 거부됩니다. 신청할 때 ``mirror`` 서비스, 공유 바디 필터는 HTML 응답에서 미러 도메인에 대한 외부 자산 URL을 다시 작성하고 CSP 빌더는 자산 지침의 미러 소스를 허용합니다."

# canonical을 노출 `cdn` 다른 역할이 그것을 통해 소비 할 수 있도록 서비스 `services.cdn`. 또한 출판 `css`
# 이름 * `javascript` canonical 참고로 aliases `cdn` 따라서 의존하는 신청은 duplicating 윤곽 없이
# 별명으로 선택될 수 있습니다.
msgid "This role deploys an Nginx-based CDN container behind the project's standard reverse proxy and exposes the canonical `cdn` service so that other roles can consume it through `services.cdn`. It also publishes the `css` and `javascript` aliases as canonical references back to `cdn` so dependent applications can opt into either alias without duplicating configuration."
msgstr ""

# canonical 노출 ``cdn`` 다른 역할이 그것을 통해 소비 할 수 있도록 서비스 ``services.cdn``. 또한 출판
# ``css`` 이름 * ``javascript`` canonical 참고로 aliases ``cdn`` 따라서 의존하는 신청은
# duplicating 윤곽 없이 별명으로 선택될 수 있습니다.
msgid "This role deploys an Nginx-based CDN container behind the project’s standard reverse proxy and exposes the canonical ``cdn`` service so that other roles can consume it through ``services.cdn``. It also publishes the ``css`` and ``javascript`` aliases as canonical references back to ``cdn`` so dependent applications can opt into either alias without duplicating configuration."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys an OpenResty container via Docker Compose, validates its configuration, and restarts it on changes."
msgstr "이 역할은 OpenResty 컨테이너를 통해 Docker Compose, 그것의 윤곽을 검증하고, 변화를 재시작합니다."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys and configures the Roulette Wheel application using Docker Compose. It pulls the latest source code from a Git repository, builds a Docker image from a configurable Node.js base, and starts the application on a user-defined local HTTP port."
msgstr "이 역할은 배포 및 구성 Roulette Wheel 사용방법 Docker Compose. 그것은 최신 소스 코드를에서 끌어 Git 저장소, configurable에서 Docker 이미지를 구축 Node.js 기본 및 사용자 정의 로컬 HTTP 포트에 응용 프로그램을 시작합니다."

msgid "This role deploys ejabberd on Docker Compose with the project's standard role-meta wiring. It binds ejabberd's `auth_method` to `svc-db-openldap` so XMPP clients authenticate against the project's central LDAP. ejabberd has no OIDC client, so the role declares no `sso` service and LDAP is its only sign-in path."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys ejabberd on Docker Compose with the project’s standard role-meta wiring. It binds ejabberd’s ``auth_method`` to ``svc-db-openldap`` so XMPP clients authenticate against the project’s central LDAP. ejabberd has no OIDC client, so the role declares no ``sso`` service and LDAP is its only sign-in path."
msgstr ""

# ``docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n`` 이미지 뒤로 PostgreSQL 관련 기사 (중앙에서 소비
# ``svc-db-postgres`` 이름 * ``sys-stk-full``). 인증은 처리됩니다 **오우즈2- 프록시** 사이드카
# (Keycloak OIDC 소개) 에서 V1, 또는 n 왼쪽8n’s 자신의 사용자 관리 UI에서 V2·8n 커뮤니티 에디션은 LDAP를
# 지원하지 않습니다 - n 뒤에 문이 있습니다.8n의 기업 라이센스 (``ldap.controller.ee.js`` CE에 등록되지 않음)
# — 그래서 LDAP 변형이 제공되지 않습니다. n 안에 저장되는 Credentials8n은 안정된 상태에서 암호화됩니다.
# ``N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY``·.
msgid "This role deploys n8n Community Edition using the upstream ``docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n`` image backed by a PostgreSQL database (consumed from the central ``svc-db-postgres`` via ``sys-stk-full``). Authentication is handled by an **oauth2-proxy** sidecar (Keycloak OIDC) in V1, or left to n8n’s own user-management UI in V2. n8n Community Edition does not support LDAP — it is gated behind n8n’s Enterprise license (``ldap.controller.ee.js`` is not registered in CE) — so no LDAP variant is offered. Credentials stored inside n8n are encrypted at rest with a stable ``N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY``."
msgstr ""

# `docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n` 이미지 뒤로 PostgreSQL 관련 기사 (중앙에서 소비 `svc-db-postgres`
# 이름 * `sys-stk-full`). 인증은 처리됩니다 **오우즈2- 프록시** 사이드카 (Keycloak OIDC 소개) 에서 V1,
# 또는 n 왼쪽8n's 자신의 사용자 관리 UI in V2·8n 커뮤니티 에디션은 LDAP를 지원하지 않습니다 - n 뒤에 문이
# 있습니다.8n's Enterprise 라이센스 (`ldap.controller.ee.js` CE에 등록되지 않음) — 그래서 LDAP
# 변형이 제공되지 않습니다. n 안에 저장되는 Credentials8n은 안정된 상태에서 암호화됩니다.
# `N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY`·.
msgid "This role deploys n8n Community Edition using the upstream `docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n` image backed by a PostgreSQL database (consumed from the central `svc-db-postgres` via `sys-stk-full`). Authentication is handled by an **oauth2-proxy** sidecar (Keycloak OIDC) in V1, or left to n8n's own user-management UI in V2. n8n Community Edition does not support LDAP — it is gated behind n8n's Enterprise license (`ldap.controller.ee.js` is not registered in CE) — so no LDAP variant is offered. Credentials stored inside n8n are encrypted at rest with a stable `N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys no AI surface and declares no ``litellm`` service, because EspoCRM’s open-source distribution does not ship one. At the pinned version ``10.0.4``, ``application/Espo/Modules`` contains only ``Crm``, ``application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json`` declares no AI key, and the release ZIP the image is built from leaves ``custom/Espo/Modules`` empty. The AI features (Summary, Intelligent Paste, AI Email Composer, AI formula functions) live exclusively in the commercial `Intelligence extension <https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/>`__, which is closed source, requires a purchased license, and is published in no ``espocrm`` GitHub repository. Bumping the version does not change this: the extension is documented as requiring EspoCRM 10.0.3 or greater, so newer cores stay hosts for it rather than absorbing it."
msgstr "이 역할은 AI 표면을 배포하고 선언하지 않습니다 ``litellm`` 서비스, 때문에 EspoCRM’ s 오픈 소스 배포 하나 발송 하지 않습니다. 핀 버전에서 ``10.0.4``· ``application/Espo/Modules`` 지원하다 ``Crm``· ``application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json`` AI 키를 선언하지 않고 ZIP 이미지는 잎에서 내장되어 있습니다. ``custom/Espo/Modules`` 한국어 AI 기능 (요약, 지능형 페이스트, AI Email Composer, AI 공식 기능) 상업적으로 살고 `Intelligence extension <https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/>`__, 닫히는 근원인, 구매한 면허를 요구하고, 안으로 간행됩니다 ``espocrm`` GitHub 저장소. 버전이 변경되지 않습니다. 확장은 필요한대로 문서화됩니다. EspoCRM 10.0.3 또는 더 중대한, 그래서 더 새로운 핵심은 그것을 흡수 보다는 오히려 호스트를 체재합니다."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys no AI surface and declares no `litellm` service, because EspoCRM's open-source distribution does not ship one. At the pinned version `10.0.4`, `application/Espo/Modules` contains only `Crm`, `application/Espo/Resources/metadata/app/config.json` declares no AI key, and the release ZIP the image is built from leaves `custom/Espo/Modules` empty. The AI features (Summary, Intelligent Paste, AI Email Composer, AI formula functions) live exclusively in the commercial [Intelligence extension](https://www.espocrm.com/extensions/intelligence/), which is closed source, requires a purchased license, and is published in no `espocrm` GitHub repository. Bumping the version does not change this: the extension is documented as requiring EspoCRM 10.0.3 or greater, so newer cores stay hosts for it rather than absorbing it."
