msgid "``sso`` renders the ``WEBLATE_SOCIAL_AUTH_OIDC_*`` backend; ``WEBLATE_REGISTRATION_ALLOW_BACKENDS=oidc`` lets a Keycloak sign-in create its account while local registration is closed. A sign-in reaches an existing account only through its ``oidc`` link keyed by the token’s ``sub``, never by e-mail: `files/python/settings_override.py <./files/python/settings_override.py>`__, mounted at ``/app/data/settings-override.py``, drops ``associate_by_email`` from the pipeline, and `files/python/adopt_admin.py <./files/python/adopt_admin.py>`__ links the administrator to the Keycloak id that `roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml <../web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml>`__ reads at deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "``sso``: the Keycloak OAuth source (``tasks/setup/oidc.yml``, removed by ``tasks/cleanup/oidc.yml`` when off). With it on, ``[oauth2_client] ENABLE_AUTO_REGISTRATION=true`` creates the Gitea account at the first sign-in and ``ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto`` links a Keycloak identity to the existing account of the same username, so directory accounts synced by the LDAP source and the platform administrator sign in through Keycloak without a link page."
