msgid "`meta/addons/` declares the curated upstream plugins. `tasks/04_addons.yml` loops the entries whose `enabled` resolves true and hands each to `tasks/utils/addon.yml`, which drops the entries this node's architecture cannot run and passes the rest to `tasks/utils/addon/runnable.yml`. An entry with a `config.archive` is installed by `tasks/utils/addon/upstream.yml` through `mmctl plugin install-url --force`; one without it falls back to `mmctl plugin marketplace install`. The entry is then enabled and its per-addon hook in `tasks/addons/` runs. Every entry is `required: false`, so a refused install emits a warning and the deploy continues."
