msgid "🛂 **Restricted access:** Only members of the ``administrator`` and ``user`` role groups sign in: the OIDC backend checks the groups claim against ``OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS``, the LDAP backend searches with a ``memberOf`` filter on both role groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "🛂 **Restricted access:** Only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups sign in: the OIDC backend checks the groups claim against `OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS`, the LDAP backend searches with a `memberOf` filter on both role groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "🛂 **Superuser reconcile:** [`files/python/reconcile_superusers.py`](./files/python/reconcile_superusers.py) grants `is_superuser` and `is_staff` to each Taiga account whose username or email matches a member of the `administrator` role group and removes both from every other account, except the bootstrap superuser and Taiga system accounts. It runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer (`tasks/03_rbac.yml`). This is the role mapping of the LDAP login path, which maps no group itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "🛂 **Superuser reconcile:** ```files/python/reconcile_superusers.py`` <./files/python/reconcile_superusers.py>`__ grants ``is_superuser`` and ``is_staff`` to each Taiga account whose username or email matches a member of the ``administrator`` role group and removes both from every other account, except the bootstrap superuser and Taiga system accounts. It runs as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer (``tasks/03_rbac.yml``). This is the role mapping of the LDAP login path, which maps no group itself."
